OL,3,GNEWSAMother writes book about murdered
OL,4,Ason to help others grieve
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mother whose son was stabbed to death
OL,7,Fin front of his own child at an east
OL,8,FLondon barber's shop has written a book
OL,9,Fabout her grief.
OL,11,FJosh McKay, 33, was attacked in Leyton
OL,12,Fin July 2024. His mother, Bash Kehinde,
OL,13,Fsaid the time since had been a "living
OL,14,Fnightmare" and the pain never went
OL,15,Faway.
OL,17,FShe hopes the book will help other
OL,18,Ffamilies coping with sudden loss.
OL,20,F"It's something that you can't shake
OL,21,Foff," she told BBC London.
